  "summary": "Adopted the content-root location design with the last-pass and agreement corrections. createEditorView over a view binds the runtime owner, reads the requested root (primary when omitted) and keeps the source view's document, sticky read-only state and authored mode; a document validates once per compiled schema. Static rendering hands render, leaf, text and decoration callbacks a cached reader of each content root and keys block reuse on root keys; one getReaderRange admission drops output for other roots before live caches, input-path fast paths and static leaf slicing, which now intersects each range with the leaf. Automatic owned-root mounts borrow the owner's decoration sources and follow its authored mode after a switch. read.list.ordinal(at) takes node targets and returns undefined for unresolved ones; path read.cell uses the cached pure grid; registry static list/table pass paths. Decoration attribute callbacks run under the read guard, and Yjs remote selections paint only in their root. Changesets, registry changelog and output, docs, Vision, Best API doctrine v253 and mirrors are updated.",
